<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vasco Núñez de Balboa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1475–1519</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vasco Núñez de Balboa was a Spanish conquistador who in 1510 founded Santa María la Antigua del Darién, the first lasting Spanish settlement on the American mainland. In September 1513 he crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isthmus-of-panama">Isthmus of Panama</a> and became the first European to see the Pacific from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, claiming it for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>. Rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedrarias-davila">Pedrarias Dávila</a>, governor of Castilla de Oro, ended with his execution for treason in 1519.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vasco-nunez-de-balboa.jpg" alt="Vasco Núñez de Balboa" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous (Spain)Unknown author after a 18th-century engraving · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Retrato_de_Vasco_Nu%C3%B1ez_de_Balboa_(1475-1517)_-_An%C3%B3nimo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
